{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792184143,"nonce":"TTYqtoz4k/IUjfwnL3AxFK2H6VE=","title":"Generic T bound to Dynamic mishandles Dynamic strings and same-module boxes","message":"Pre-existing at e313dbad (checked by stash/build/pop A/B).\n\n    static function same\u003cT\u003e(a:T, b:T) { trace(a); trace(b); }\n    var d:Dynamic = \"test\";\n    same(d, d);        // prints pointers, not \"test\"\n    same(d, \"test\");   // SIGSEGV\n\nRelated: a box passed to a same-module generic method specialised for a\nscalar T (`eqn(d, 12)` with d a Dynamic Int from Reflect.field) reaches\nthe body as the raw box pointer. `normalize_dynamic_args_for_erased_formals`\n(mir/types.rs) only runs for callees in `external_function_param_types`,\nso local callees skip it; the cross-module path (unit.Test.eq) works.\n\nA TAST-level unbox of Dynamic arguments bound to a scalar T fixes the\nlocal case but lost 12 rows: those arguments are usually decayed Dynamic\n(erased generic returns, Array\u003cDynamic\u003e of raw ints), not boxes.","files":null}]}